WEBVTT

00:04.963 --> 00:08.341
<i>This was the moment
that I learned two things.</i>

00:09.843 --> 00:12.846
<i>That you don't realize
what's important to you until it's gone.</i>

00:13.513 --> 00:14.514
<i>And that...</i>

00:15.306 --> 00:18.184
<i>it's only too easy to lose.</i>

00:23.648 --> 00:25.191
<i>And that made me scared.</i>

00:25.775 --> 00:27.902
<i>Even if I bonded
with something precious to me...</i>

00:27.986 --> 00:30.196
<i>wouldn't I just lose it again?</i>

00:31.114 --> 00:32.282
<i>Just thinking that...</i>

00:41.666 --> 00:42.667
Don't worry.

00:43.376 --> 00:45.336
I'm not going anywhere.

00:55.055 --> 00:57.974
YOZAKURA FAMILY

00:59.142 --> 01:03.021
PLAN 1
THE CHERRY BLOSSOM RING

01:05.523 --> 01:07.067
All right! Lunchtime!

01:07.150 --> 01:08.359
Let's go to the cafeteria!

01:09.444 --> 01:10.820
Asano!

01:10.904 --> 01:13.865
Listen, we've got
a practice soccer match coming up.

01:13.948 --> 01:15.241
Help us out!

01:15.325 --> 01:17.577
Hey, how about a study group at my house?

01:17.660 --> 01:19.287
Let's go to karaoke after school!

01:19.829 --> 01:21.289
Asano!

01:23.166 --> 01:25.752
S-Sorry. Can't do it.

01:25.877 --> 01:28.671
Oh, crap, he turned us down again!

01:28.880 --> 01:30.757
What's this, our tenth straight fail?

01:30.840 --> 01:33.510
You play harder to get
than any girl, Asano.

01:33.593 --> 01:36.805
Asano! We've been in the same class
for a month now.

01:36.888 --> 01:38.306
Let's hang out!

01:38.389 --> 01:40.058
It makes us sad, you know!

01:40.141 --> 01:42.018
Hey, better back off now.

01:42.102 --> 01:44.604
- Huh? Why is that?
- Look at him.

01:46.356 --> 01:48.900
He's so nervous, he's blacked out.

01:48.983 --> 01:51.402
Answering us that first time
must have wiped him out.

01:51.486 --> 01:55.907
I thought that he would
have come around a little after a month.

01:55.990 --> 01:59.410
You have to feel sorry
for anyone who's that shy, huh?

01:59.494 --> 02:01.079
Yup.

02:01.663 --> 02:04.833
<i>The thing is,
it's not like I'm shy or anything.</i>

02:04.916 --> 02:06.835
<i>I'm happy that they asked me to hang out,</i>

02:06.918 --> 02:09.212
<i>and it would be great
to talk about stuff with them.</i>

02:09.295 --> 02:10.296
<i>But...</i>

02:11.089 --> 02:12.173
Forget it.

02:12.257 --> 02:14.134
Let's try again tomorrow, okay?

02:15.885 --> 02:17.554
You turned them down again?

02:19.472 --> 02:20.849
Mutsumi.

02:21.432 --> 02:23.643
But they were nice enough to ask you!

02:23.726 --> 02:25.854
Who cares? Just leave me alone!

02:26.354 --> 02:28.648
- I made us lunch, so let's eat!
- No, I'm--

02:28.731 --> 02:32.193
I know you haven't been eating right
because you're always working!

02:32.277 --> 02:35.280
I've got some of that salty <i>tamagoyaki</i>
that you like, Taiyo.

02:35.363 --> 02:38.241
And, hey, if you leave your carrots
again, you'll live to regret it!

02:41.202 --> 02:42.370
Yes, ma'am.

02:42.704 --> 02:43.788
That's my boy!

02:44.622 --> 02:46.749
Wow, can you believe Yozakura?

02:47.250 --> 02:51.171
Still, why would the idol of this school,
Yozakura, do that?

02:51.254 --> 02:53.423
I hear that those two
are childhood friends.

02:53.506 --> 02:55.341
I-I'm so jealous.

02:57.093 --> 02:58.928
Look at you, always alone.

02:59.012 --> 03:03.266
It worries me, thinking that you could
spend the rest of your life like this!

03:03.766 --> 03:05.560
Who are you, my mom?

03:06.311 --> 03:11.107
Who are you to talk? Didn't you
turn down that third-year, Tanaka?

03:11.191 --> 03:13.401
Huh? Oh, yeah.

03:13.484 --> 03:16.988
He's smart, he's good-looking, and he's
the captain of the soccer team, right?

03:17.071 --> 03:18.281
I mean, what's not to like?

03:18.364 --> 03:21.784
Oh?
And who are you, Taiyo, my father?

03:21.868 --> 03:24.245
Hey, wipe that smug look
off your face!

03:24.746 --> 03:26.456
Never mind about me, okay?

03:26.539 --> 03:30.543
What you need to do is to finally
move on, or your parents will be sad.

03:30.627 --> 03:33.630
So that's why you need
to rehab your communication skills.

03:33.713 --> 03:34.923
Here! Say "ahh."

03:35.423 --> 03:37.133
How is this rehab?

03:37.634 --> 03:38.885
Never mind! Just eat!

03:39.844 --> 03:41.137
Ahh...

03:41.221 --> 03:42.847
Ahh!

03:42.931 --> 03:45.558
So tasty!

03:46.309 --> 03:48.311
M-Mr. Hirukawa?

03:48.394 --> 03:51.522
Come on! You promised
to stop snacking, remember?

03:52.023 --> 03:53.483
Hey, my bad.

03:53.566 --> 03:56.819
My body reacted
to the scent of your <i>tamagoyaki.</i>

03:57.320 --> 03:59.197
Hmm? What's wrong, Asano?

03:59.280 --> 04:00.949
Uh... Nothing.

04:01.032 --> 04:02.992
<i>Where did he come from? Out of nowhere?</i>

04:03.493 --> 04:07.622
Mr. Hirukawa, aren't you supposed to be
on a business trip overseas for a lecture?

04:07.705 --> 04:10.291
Well, I missed
your lunches so much, Mutsumi,

04:10.375 --> 04:13.002
that I changed my schedule
to come home earlier.

04:13.086 --> 04:14.545
Oh.

04:15.088 --> 04:18.675
Still, I have to say that white streak
is as gorgeous as ever!

04:18.758 --> 04:20.093
I wanna rub my cheek against it!

04:20.176 --> 04:21.469
Do that, and I'll report you!

04:21.552 --> 04:24.681
If you're done here, please go back
to the vice principal's office.

04:24.764 --> 04:27.725
Huh? Oh, but I'm not.
I'm so not done here yet!

04:28.309 --> 04:31.271
Hey, Asano,
come to my office when school's out.

04:31.354 --> 04:33.439
Huh? Y-You mean me?

04:33.523 --> 04:34.649
That's right.

04:34.732 --> 04:37.193
Uh... Did I do something?

04:37.277 --> 04:38.903
Right, see you later!

04:38.987 --> 04:40.154
Hey, wait--

04:41.197 --> 04:43.449
What's the deal with that guy?

04:50.540 --> 04:52.083
See ya, Asano!

04:52.750 --> 04:55.044
Uh... S-See you.

04:55.128 --> 04:57.672
- Hey, let's hit the karaoke booth!
- Hey, sounds good!

04:57.755 --> 04:58.923
What should we sing?

04:59.007 --> 05:01.634
A medley of this season's
opening themes, what else?

05:10.059 --> 05:15.440
<i>Ever since that day, I've been
afraid to connect with other people.</i>

05:15.523 --> 05:17.317
VICE PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE
HIRUKAWA'S ROOM

05:22.322 --> 05:24.115
E-Excuse me!

05:24.991 --> 05:27.660
Hey, you're here?
I've been waiting for you!

05:33.666 --> 05:35.501
<i>T-Too close.</i>

05:35.960 --> 05:39.213
Um, what exactly am I here for?

05:39.297 --> 05:43.301
Oh, well... I really wanted
to show you my collection, see.

05:43.384 --> 05:44.677
Collection?

05:45.303 --> 05:48.681
Ta-da!
My "secret shots of Mutsumi" collection!

05:48.765 --> 05:49.932
<i>Huh? What a pervert!</i>

05:50.058 --> 05:53.019
I want your evaluation
as her childhood friend.

05:53.478 --> 05:57.148
<i>I mean, I knew Mutsumi
was a favorite of Mr. Hirukawa's, but...</i>

05:57.690 --> 05:59.734
See, look! This is my personal favorite!

06:01.778 --> 06:04.238
<i>He's a lost cause.
This is pathetic.</i>

06:04.322 --> 06:06.199
<i>I guess I'd better report him.</i>

06:06.282 --> 06:08.034
Y-Yes, it's nice.

06:08.534 --> 06:10.119
Hey, how about this one?

06:10.203 --> 06:12.121
Mutsumi playing Sevens at home!

06:12.205 --> 06:13.206
Isn't she cute?

06:13.331 --> 06:14.791
<i>What?</i>

06:14.874 --> 06:17.627
Hey, here she is at five.
I took this at the park.

06:17.710 --> 06:19.045
Brings back memories.

06:19.128 --> 06:20.546
<i>Ugh!</i>

06:21.297 --> 06:24.217
Aww... This is the one I took
when she was three,

06:24.300 --> 06:25.635
at her <i>Shichigosan</i> celebration.

06:25.718 --> 06:27.136
What an angel!

06:27.220 --> 06:31.599
<i>Huh? Why would a teacher
like him have pictures like these?</i>

06:32.767 --> 06:34.018
You see...

06:34.102 --> 06:37.522
I've been watching over Mutsumi
from the shadows all this time.

06:38.189 --> 06:41.275
Since Mutsumi is so gorgeous,
to shield her from all the undesirables,

06:41.359 --> 06:43.403
I've been keeping
an eye on her constantly,

06:43.486 --> 06:44.946
nonstop, without a break.

06:45.530 --> 06:48.157
That third-year kid, Tanaka,
was pretty pesky yesterday,

06:48.241 --> 06:51.327
but when I graciously asked him
to stay away from Mutsumi,

06:51.411 --> 06:53.913
he gladly agreed to comply in the end.

06:54.997 --> 06:58.167
<i>Go on.
Once more, in a great big voice.</i>

06:58.251 --> 07:01.879
<i>I-I'll never go near Yozakura again!</i>

07:02.296 --> 07:04.507
<i>This dude... He's totally insane!</i>

07:04.590 --> 07:06.717
<i>I've got to do something,
or Mutsumi will--</i>

07:06.801 --> 07:08.678
I envy you, Asano.

07:08.761 --> 07:11.806
Getting those homemade lunches
from Mutsumi...

07:14.517 --> 07:18.396
I've been looking the other way
since you're Mutsumi's childhood friend,

07:18.479 --> 07:21.315
but things have changed,
and that just won't be possible now.

07:21.399 --> 07:22.400
<i>Damn it!</i>

07:22.483 --> 07:25.361
<i>I can't make a sound.
My legs are frozen, too.</i>

07:26.195 --> 07:28.823
<i>Mutsumi's in danger, but I...</i>

07:28.906 --> 07:30.491
Don't take it personally.

07:30.575 --> 07:32.785
This is all for the sake
of my beloved kid sister.

07:32.869 --> 07:34.162
<i>Huh?</i>

07:35.496 --> 07:36.956
Stop it right there.

07:37.165 --> 07:38.166
Huh?

07:40.168 --> 07:41.878
VICE PRINCIPAL'S OFFICE
HIRUKAWA'S ROOM

07:57.852 --> 07:59.729
Hey, you're awake!

08:00.229 --> 08:01.647
Morning, Taiyo!

08:02.190 --> 08:03.691
Mutsumi?

08:03.774 --> 08:05.818
Glad to see you're all right.

08:15.953 --> 08:17.330
Wh-Who are you?

08:17.413 --> 08:21.375
Taiyo, it's all right! Look, it's me!

08:21.876 --> 08:26.047
Nanao, there's no way
you're hiding all that behind Mutsumi.

08:26.130 --> 08:28.799
M-Mutsumi! Who are these people?

08:28.883 --> 08:31.010
Well, it's kind of a long story.

08:31.636 --> 08:33.971
But for now, let me introduce them to you.

08:34.472 --> 08:36.349
These are my siblings.

08:37.016 --> 08:39.101
S-Siblings?

08:44.774 --> 08:46.817
This is my big sister, Futaba.

08:47.318 --> 08:48.319
Nice to meet you.

08:48.903 --> 08:51.280
And this my big brother, Shinzo.

08:51.364 --> 08:52.990
N-Nice to meet you.

08:53.658 --> 08:55.284
This is Big Sis Shion.

08:55.368 --> 08:56.619
Yo.

08:57.453 --> 08:59.830
And Kengo.
- Hey there.

09:00.581 --> 09:01.749
And Nanao!

09:01.832 --> 09:03.543
H-Hello!

09:04.377 --> 09:06.837
And this is our guard dog, Goliath!

09:07.380 --> 09:10.800
As you can see, we're a family of spies!

09:11.801 --> 09:14.804
It was really tough, keeping my mouth shut
about that for ten-plus years.

09:14.887 --> 09:15.888
What a relief!

09:15.972 --> 09:17.723
Hold up! Hold up! Hold up!

09:17.807 --> 09:19.267
Spies? What are you talking about?

09:19.350 --> 09:22.478
I can't process that like you'd said,
"We're a family of greengrocers!"

09:22.562 --> 09:24.981
It's just that
instead of eggplants and radishes,

09:25.064 --> 09:27.108
we deal in guns and intel.
Isn't it kinda the same?

09:27.191 --> 09:29.610
Not at all! It's totally different!

09:29.694 --> 09:33.447
I know! I'm getting pranked.
You're pranking me, right, Mutsumi?

09:33.531 --> 09:35.199
Like, this gun is just a toy, right?

09:35.283 --> 09:36.325
Hey, watch out!

09:39.036 --> 09:41.914
Well, hey.
Unlike in books and movies,

09:41.998 --> 09:43.874
being a spy is just
a common, ordinary job.

09:43.958 --> 09:47.169
Lately, there's been a surge
in cheap public-servant spies,

09:47.253 --> 09:49.839
so as freelancers,
we can't compete, can we?

09:49.922 --> 09:51.382
Oh, we'll be fine.

09:51.465 --> 09:55.344
I mean, we do lead the rankings
on the review sites, with 4.8 stars.

09:55.845 --> 09:58.973
<i>Reviews for spies?
Isn't that a huge info leak?</i>

10:00.516 --> 10:04.687
True that. And we've got Big Bro Kyoichiro
to boost our popularity.

10:05.438 --> 10:09.317
The undisputed number one "Male Spy That
Female Spies Want to Be Targeted By"!

10:09.400 --> 10:12.445
Well, he's also number one
in hate-thread size by a mile.

10:12.945 --> 10:15.406
What? Mr. Hirukawa?

10:15.489 --> 10:16.949
You know him, right?

10:17.450 --> 10:19.785
The eldest son
of the Yozakura family, Kyoichiro.

10:19.869 --> 10:22.079
As a person, he's flawed,
but in every other aspect,

10:22.163 --> 10:26.167
combat power, intelligence,
he's the best spy in our family.

10:26.250 --> 10:29.420
B-But why would your brother target me?

10:29.962 --> 10:31.756
Because we got a tip...

10:31.839 --> 10:35.718
that someone was plotting to kill Mutsumi.

10:35.801 --> 10:38.721
Hold on a second! I would never...

10:39.221 --> 10:43.184
Well, we did get the intel
from that moronic social media post.

10:43.684 --> 10:46.062
Huh? Social... media?

10:46.604 --> 10:48.230
<i>Spies on social media?</i>

10:48.314 --> 10:50.441
<i>Not only that, they've got
a ton of followers too!</i>

10:52.526 --> 10:54.695
Years ago, during a certain incident...

10:55.196 --> 10:57.823
<i>Mutsumi suffered a near-fatal injury
because of Kyoichiro.</i>

10:58.324 --> 11:01.410
<i>That white hair is a remnant
of the stress from that accident.</i>

11:02.119 --> 11:03.996
<i>Ever since then, his sense of guilt</i>

11:04.080 --> 11:06.791
<i>has made him obsess over Mutsumi
to an abnormal degree.</i>

11:07.291 --> 11:09.502
<i>He's changed his name and job
so he can surveil her,</i>

11:09.585 --> 11:11.253
<i>and he'll interfere with everything,</i>

11:11.337 --> 11:13.673
<i>from her daily life
to her personal connections.</i>

11:13.756 --> 11:16.592
<i>He's turned into
a Mutsumi-protecting monster.</i>

11:17.551 --> 11:18.928
<i>Despite his hatred for you,</i>

11:19.011 --> 11:21.639
<i>he's always given you a pass
as Mutsumi's childhood friend.</i>

11:21.722 --> 11:25.059
<i>But now he has a reason
to justify getting rid of you.</i>

11:27.395 --> 11:29.897
I really am sorry
that my brother is such an idiot.

11:30.398 --> 11:32.608
Oh... no... uh...

11:33.901 --> 11:36.195
Whoops. Speak of the devil.

11:36.278 --> 11:37.697
Wh-What's going on?

11:37.780 --> 11:40.700
Kyoichiro has
just returned to this house.

11:41.200 --> 11:43.327
He probably means to finish you off.

11:44.495 --> 11:45.955
Now, now, calm down.

11:46.539 --> 11:49.417
After all,
you're safest with us, you know.

11:50.042 --> 11:51.460
Shion, Shinzo...

11:52.795 --> 11:56.006
Every door leading
to this room has been locked.

11:56.090 --> 11:58.426
And I've set every trap
we have on hand.

11:59.385 --> 12:02.471
There's no getting through to that guy,
so what can we do?

12:02.555 --> 12:05.850
All right, you guys, we're going to
give that moron a beatdown!

12:05.933 --> 12:07.768
B-Beatdown?

12:07.852 --> 12:09.979
Well, not that
the odds are on our side.

12:10.062 --> 12:14.108
Even at five to one, our win rate
for past head-on clashes was a mere 30%.

12:14.191 --> 12:17.653
There's also a 42% chance of one of us
needing six months of recovery

12:17.737 --> 12:20.030
and a 25% chance
of the house burning down.

12:20.114 --> 12:23.576
Well, then, we should just
look at it as an early renovation!

12:29.540 --> 12:32.960
B-But... it would be
because of me. That's too...

12:33.043 --> 12:35.087
It's always been a family issue.

12:35.171 --> 12:36.547
Don't give it a second thought.

12:39.925 --> 12:43.012
There's just one way
for you to survive this.

12:43.095 --> 12:44.096
What?

12:44.889 --> 12:46.432
Hey... Big Sis!

12:46.932 --> 12:49.518
You two need to get married.

12:50.019 --> 12:52.313
M-Married?

12:54.064 --> 12:55.441
Look at that steam.

12:55.524 --> 12:57.234
Well, who can blame him?

12:57.318 --> 12:58.319
HEALTH FIRST

12:58.402 --> 13:01.447
If you marry into our family,
in accordance with our one rule...

13:01.530 --> 13:02.531
PEACE IN THE HOUSEHOLD

13:02.615 --> 13:05.659
"No killing among family members,"
your life, at least, can be preserved.

13:06.285 --> 13:09.121
You only have to exchange rings
to marry a Yozakura.

13:09.705 --> 13:12.041
This Cherry Blossom Ring is double-banded.

13:12.541 --> 13:16.128
<i>The moment you give half to your spouse,
your marriage becomes official.</i>

13:17.129 --> 13:20.299
Even that idiot isn't stupid enough
to break such an ironclad rule.

13:20.382 --> 13:22.176
And I think it'll be a good chance for him

13:22.259 --> 13:24.845
to finally get over his sister fetish.

13:25.346 --> 13:27.973
Well, that's just what I personally hope.

13:28.474 --> 13:31.435
To protect you and to protect Mutsumi.

13:32.019 --> 13:33.979
Not a bad idea, wouldn't you agree?

13:34.605 --> 13:36.649
<i>Me and Mutsumi, get married?</i>

13:37.650 --> 13:38.651
<i>Marriage...</i>

13:39.527 --> 13:40.861
<i>family.</i>

13:47.326 --> 13:48.828
No.

13:48.911 --> 13:50.538
I'm not marrying Taiyo.

13:51.038 --> 13:52.248
Mutsumi...

13:52.331 --> 13:55.918
I'm sorry, Big Sis Futaba.
I know you're looking out for us.

13:56.460 --> 14:00.339
But you know, right?
That Taiyo's lost his family.

14:00.422 --> 14:03.634
Even now, he can't talk to people
or even sleep.

14:03.717 --> 14:06.428
He's still coming to terms
with the loss of his family.

14:06.512 --> 14:09.265
No one knows better than Taiyo
what that pain is like,

14:09.348 --> 14:11.892
so casually telling him,
"Join our family..."

14:11.976 --> 14:13.686
that would be too cruel.

14:14.395 --> 14:15.396
<i>Mutsumi...</i>

14:16.730 --> 14:17.815
Gotcha.

14:18.858 --> 14:20.985
Sorry to be so insensitive.

14:21.485 --> 14:23.529
No, no, it's all right.

14:23.612 --> 14:24.780
<i>What's going on?</i>

14:24.864 --> 14:27.408
<i>Why am I feeling so conflicted?</i>

14:28.826 --> 14:30.536
Okay! Now that that's settled,

14:30.619 --> 14:33.539
let's do our best
to clobber that stupid eldest son!

14:33.622 --> 14:34.957
Yeah!

14:35.457 --> 14:36.750
What about strategy?

14:36.834 --> 14:38.210
Huh? Can't we just wing it?

14:38.294 --> 14:41.255
Sorry to drag you
into our family problems, Taiyo.

14:41.839 --> 14:44.008
I-I'm getting nervous.

14:44.091 --> 14:46.635
Hey, it's gonna be okay, Big Bro Shinzo.

14:46.719 --> 14:48.929
Leaving me out, so cruel of you.

14:49.430 --> 14:51.056
Let me join in on the fun!

14:54.226 --> 14:56.353
So? Who are we clobbering?

14:56.437 --> 14:57.771
<i>Wh-When did he get here?</i>

14:57.855 --> 14:59.106
Oh, hey, Shinzo.

14:59.189 --> 15:01.817
You renovated the traps
around the mansion, right?

15:01.901 --> 15:04.194
Well, evading them was a pain,
so I destroyed them all.

15:04.278 --> 15:05.279
My bad.

15:05.362 --> 15:06.614
S-Seriously?

15:09.617 --> 15:11.952
I'm only going to warn you once.

15:12.036 --> 15:14.496
Back off from these two, Kyoichiro.

15:14.580 --> 15:15.706
No can do.

15:15.789 --> 15:17.666
There's no guarantee that he's harmless,

15:17.750 --> 15:21.962
and for Mutsumi's sake, "guilty until
proven innocent" is how I roll!

15:23.756 --> 15:25.257
If you have a problem with that,

15:25.341 --> 15:26.926
as Yozakura, you can use force to...

15:27.009 --> 15:29.261
That's what
we're going to do, all right.

15:37.269 --> 15:39.438
All right. Time for a sibling fight!

15:44.026 --> 15:45.361
Sorry, Big Bro!

15:49.156 --> 15:50.157
Whoa.

15:51.158 --> 15:52.701
Sorry, Nanao.

15:52.785 --> 15:55.496
Big Bro is busy, so let's play later.

15:56.622 --> 15:58.332
Shinzo! Nanao! Get out of the way!

16:08.092 --> 16:10.302
That was pretty good teamwork, you know.

16:10.386 --> 16:13.305
But you left yourselves
way too open after that one strike.

16:13.389 --> 16:16.558
Now, enough with the training.
Just hand over that guy.

16:17.059 --> 16:20.813
Otherwise... I'm going to
rip this house to shreds.

16:20.896 --> 16:22.690
Wh-What's that?

16:22.773 --> 16:25.818
His special weapon, Steel Spider.

16:25.901 --> 16:30.072
Mutsumi, we're going to buy you some time,
so you take that kid and run!

16:42.751 --> 16:43.961
What?

16:44.044 --> 16:46.463
Let me go, damn it,
you jerk-ass eldest son!

16:47.047 --> 16:49.800
Don't rage like that, Futaba,
or your body will get julienned!

16:49.883 --> 16:51.093
Damn it!

16:51.176 --> 16:53.053
Hey, Kengo, what are you waiting for?

16:53.137 --> 16:54.596
Okay.

16:54.680 --> 16:56.390
Both of you, this way.

16:56.473 --> 16:58.684
This game is impossible
at your skill level, Shion.

16:58.767 --> 17:00.060
Shut up, perv.

17:00.144 --> 17:02.438
I don't care if it's
an impossible game or a crap one!

17:08.944 --> 17:12.072
For a real gamer,
fun means pulling out all the stops!

17:12.656 --> 17:13.782
That's so cool!

17:24.209 --> 17:26.211
A-Are they okay? The others?

17:26.295 --> 17:28.756
Yes. Remember what Big Sis Futaba said?

17:28.839 --> 17:32.301
We're not allowed to kill
any family members, so it's all good.

17:32.384 --> 17:33.469
B-But...

17:34.053 --> 17:37.347
Don't worry about it. Come on.
You need to hide now, Taiyo.

17:53.322 --> 17:56.617
Don't worry. I'm not going anywhere.

18:03.624 --> 18:07.086
How pesky were those drones?

18:07.628 --> 18:09.755
All right, come over here, Mutsumi.

18:09.838 --> 18:12.716
I wouldn't want to soil you
with his blood splatter.

18:17.513 --> 18:19.431
There you go. That's a good girl.

18:20.057 --> 18:23.018
Now, then,
dive into your big brother's arms!

18:33.403 --> 18:35.447
Awesome disguise there, Kengo.

18:35.531 --> 18:38.033
Right down to the same number
of eyelashes. I'm impressed!

18:39.368 --> 18:41.995
Whoops. You got me.

18:42.079 --> 18:45.457
But you still haven't mastered
the art of disguising others.

18:48.544 --> 18:49.962
Come on, Mutsumi.

18:50.045 --> 18:52.923
Be a good girl,
and tell me where you hid him.

18:53.966 --> 18:56.343
<i>Damn it. What should I do?</i>

18:56.426 --> 18:57.845
<i>Listen up, Taiyo.</i>

18:57.928 --> 19:00.806
<i>Whatever happens,
don't ever come out of there, all right?</i>

19:01.974 --> 19:04.434
Big Bro!
Stop this nonsense already!

19:05.769 --> 19:07.980
I'm telling you,
Taiyo's not trying to kill me!

19:08.063 --> 19:10.899
You know all about it, too, don't you?
About Taiyo's family?

19:10.983 --> 19:13.777
So please don't hurt Taiyo anymore.

19:15.696 --> 19:19.408
All right, fine, Mutsumi.
I won't lay a hand on him anymore.

19:20.033 --> 19:21.034
Big Bro...

19:21.118 --> 19:24.496
And I'm also not going
to let you out of the house anymore.

19:24.580 --> 19:25.622
What?

19:25.706 --> 19:27.833
Out there,
you'll attract the unsavory,

19:27.916 --> 19:29.793
and I'll have failed you
as your big brother.

19:29.877 --> 19:34.006
From now on, I'm going to do much,
much more to keep you safe, all right?

19:34.089 --> 19:35.090
Big Bro.

19:35.591 --> 19:38.093
It's dangerous,
so you don't need to go outside.

19:38.177 --> 19:40.554
The Internet is dangerous too,
so no smartphone for you.

19:40.637 --> 19:44.183
I'm going to rid the world of everything
that could put you in danger.

19:44.683 --> 19:49.396
School, your friends, fun, romance,
I'll get rid of them all.

19:49.479 --> 19:51.356
I'll eliminate all that's unnecessary

19:51.440 --> 19:53.775
so you can have
a safe, peaceful household.

19:53.859 --> 19:58.363
Ah, just imagining it
makes my heart flutter!

19:58.447 --> 20:01.074
The day that I nearly lost you,
I vowed to accept any kind of pain

20:02.242 --> 20:04.620
if only I could keep this child safe.

20:05.120 --> 20:08.790
I would give up my own life
in order to protect you, my beloved.

20:09.541 --> 20:11.043
Now then, Mutsumi...

20:11.543 --> 20:14.922
forget about that guy,
and let's live in peace.

20:16.173 --> 20:17.382
Okay.

20:17.466 --> 20:19.343
<i>Sorry... Taiyo.</i>

20:21.762 --> 20:23.847
Taiyo.

20:24.932 --> 20:26.350
Let Mutsumi go.

20:26.433 --> 20:28.352
I have no use for you anymore.

20:28.435 --> 20:31.563
Kindly refrain from sticking your nose
in my family's business.

20:31.647 --> 20:34.107
<i>This guy is probably just like me.</i>

20:34.650 --> 20:36.652
<i>He's afraid to lose
what's precious to him.</i>

20:37.152 --> 20:41.281
<i>But making the precious person
he wants to protect look like that...</i>

20:41.907 --> 20:43.158
<i>I just know that's wrong!</i>

20:43.742 --> 20:44.743
Mutsumi...

20:45.244 --> 20:46.245
Let's do it.

20:46.328 --> 20:49.039
That method that your sister said
would keep both of us safe.

20:49.122 --> 20:51.166
But...

20:51.875 --> 20:53.460
I'll be fine.

20:53.543 --> 20:57.422
Because you promised me
that you weren't going anywhere.

21:00.300 --> 21:01.385
Okay.

21:16.483 --> 21:17.859
Well, that was close.

21:17.943 --> 21:20.779
Damn that Futaba,
putting ideas in your heads.

21:20.862 --> 21:24.324
But there's no chance in hell
that I'd ever let you do that.

21:28.078 --> 21:30.289
<i>Hey, Mutsumi...</i>

21:30.372 --> 21:34.376
<i>thanks for always protecting
the hopeless wreck that I am.</i>

21:35.252 --> 21:36.336
That's why...

21:36.420 --> 21:38.046
from now on...

21:38.130 --> 21:41.174
I'm going to be the one to protect you!

21:47.306 --> 21:48.765
Are you both okay?

21:52.644 --> 21:55.689
I promise you,
I'm going to protect Mutsumi.

21:56.606 --> 21:57.733
Nice to meet you...

21:58.233 --> 22:00.068
Big Bro Kyoichiro!

22:00.485 --> 22:02.112
I-Impossible!

22:05.282 --> 22:06.283
Taiyo!

22:13.040 --> 22:14.833
All right!

22:14.916 --> 22:16.626
Hey, pretty good!

22:17.502 --> 22:20.047
Yeah, he sure is... awesome.

22:20.672 --> 22:23.050
You're so cool, Taiyo!

22:25.635 --> 22:30.974
Too bad for you, Kyoichiro.
But there's no time to be melancholy.

22:32.309 --> 22:34.686
- You did it! Good for you! Congrats!
- Wow! Amazing!

22:34.770 --> 22:38.899
You've got to teach that kid.
Protecting Mutsumi...

22:39.775 --> 22:41.902
what that really means.

24:07.904 --> 24:10.824
NEXT TIME
THE YOZAKURAS' LIFELINE
